{
 "_meta": {
  "source": "Matter per-device diagnostics (data.node.attributes 0/53/*, 0/51/0) + ha_get_device node_diagnostics + thread integration diagnostics (border routers only)",
  "capture_date": "2026-11-06",
  "notes": [
   "Attribute keys are endpoint/cluster/attribute; table entries keep Matter spec field ids as string keys.",
   "0/53/7 fields: 0 ExtAddress, 1 Age, 2 Rloc16, 3 LinkFrameCounter, 4 MleFrameCounter, 5 LQI(0-3), 6 AverageRssi, 7 LastRssi, 8 FrameErrorRate, 9 MessageErrorRate, 10 RxOnWhenIdle, 11 FullThreadDevice, 12 FullNetworkData, 13 IsChild.",
   "0/53/8 fields: 0 ExtAddress, 1 Rloc16, 2 RouterId, 3 NextHop, 4 PathCost, 5 LQIIn, 6 LQIOut, 7 Age, 8 Allocated, 9 LinkEstablished.",
   "own_rloc16 is derived from the mesh-local RLOC IPv6 (...:0:ff:fe00:XXXX) in 0/51/0 field 6; join neighbors/routes on Rloc16.",
   "ExtAddress values are fake. In the raw capture the 64-bit table values had float precision loss; they were mapped to the owning device's fake ext address when within 4096 of an exact own address, otherwise to a fake 0x00000B... value. Own addresses (0/51/0 field 4, node_diagnostics.mac_address) are exact fakes in the 0x00000A... range.",
   "Fake IPv6: mesh-local prefix fd00:0:<net>::/64 keeps the real RLOC IID (so derivation still works); link-local derived from the fake ext address; other addresses get counter IIDs.",
   "0/53/0, 0/53/2, 0/53/3 for devices with attrs_fetched_individually not listing them were filled from network constants, not fetched per device.",
   "is_shadow_record: disabled duplicate registry entries created by a time-sync helper integration with the same node_id as a real device; they have no diagnostics.",
   "Bridge (ethernet) node has no 0/53 cluster; its non-Thread interfaces had MAC/IPs replaced and IP lists emptied."
  ]
 },
